        "title": "Redis - Commands, Data Structures, and Modules",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Redis is not a query language in the SQL sense — it's a command-based interface to in-memory data structures. It's the standard ephemeral store: cache, session store, rate limiter, pub/sub bus, distributed lock, leaderboard. Redis Stack adds modules: RediSearch (full-text + vector search), RedisJSON, RedisTimeSeries, RedisBloom. The \"query language\" is the combination of commands + Lua scripting for atomicity."
